  "implementation": [
    "Reusable host GuestInput32 performs the existing kernel PID/UID plus lifetime-descriptor handshake, serializes touch and key events, and shares InputCommandQueue MOVE coalescing without crossing gesture/key boundaries.",
    "InputControl32 validates keyboard packets and forwards real KeyEvents to stock IInputManager with the guest virtual-keyboard map, action, repeat count, timestamps and modifier state.",
    "The ordinary test app records real onPause/onResume state, process-start counters distinct from activity recreation, acknowledged clicks, EditText text changes and received key-up events.",
    "The driver waits for stable current-layout pixel proof, rechecks layout after its screenshot, sends three separately acknowledged button taps and an editor-focus tap, then types a12b, deletes one character and types 9 through the actual host view. It requires guest text a129 and the final key-up. It does not retry unacknowledged taps."
  ],
